My apologies for the outburst. Your edits are mostly sound, and I appreciate that. But on that day there were some very odd edits that made me concerned (actually only two, but it seemed much more at the time):

On lamji:
   Word: immediate, In Sense: happening right away
But "lamji" refers to something that is next to something else in a sequence, not something that happens right away.

On bapli:
   Place Keywords:
   Word: effect, In Sense: result, For Place: 1
But the x1 of bapli is not an effect, it is more like a cause. If anything in bapli is an effect, it is the x2.

Soon after that, I discovered your earlier edit for culno, which is equally perplexing:
   Word: whole, In Sense: entirety, For Place: 1
Was this change meant to be on mulno?

